# Deploy after changes

`.cursor/hooks/commit-and-push.sh` runs on agent `stop` and commits leftover changes, then `git push`. Do not duplicate that in the agent unless you still have uncommitted work at the end of the turn.

If you do commit yourself:

1. `git add` changed files (never `.clasp.json`, `.clasprc.json`, secrets, or credentials)
2. `git commit` with a short message focused on why
3. `git push`

`clasp push` runs automatically in GitHub Actions on push to `main` (see `.github/workflows/clasp-push.yml`); do not run `clasp push` locally.

If there are no changes to commit, skip git steps.
